    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d477">

                <pb facs="0641" n="627" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 PW/6–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Brazilian Acting Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Macedo Soares</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Acting Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-06">June 6, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have the honor to communicate to Your Excellency that the Brazilian Government,
                    having for some time considered the aggression <pb facs="0642" n="628"
                        xml:id="pg628"/> of Japan against the United States of America as though it
                    were directed against Brazil itself and desiring to cooperate for the final
                    victory of the United Nations and their allies, resolved by a Decree dated today
                    to declare the existence of a state of war with the above mentioned aggressor
                    power.</p>
                <p>I take this opportunity to renew to Your Excellency Brazil’s confidence in the
                    triumph over the common enemy.</p>
                <p>Cordial salutations.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d477-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">José Roberto de Macedo Soares</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d477-f1" n="34" xml:id="d477-f1-content">
                <p>For text of reply to this telegram by the Acting Secretary of State and a
                    statement issued by him on June 6, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi> June 10, 1945, p. 1061.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
